[
    {
        "content": "<p>Based on <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"111080\">@Floris van Doorn</span> suggestion here is an experimental tactic <code>make_have</code> that is meant to be run as discharger in <code>simp</code> or <code>fun_prop</code> that will give you code action to add <code>have : &lt;hypothesis&gt; := sorry</code> before <code>simp</code> or <code>fun_prop</code>.</p>\n<p>You can write</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">disch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">assumption</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">make_have</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>get code action</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Code</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">action</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>after clicking on it you get</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">disch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">assumption</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">make_have</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Here is the full code (mostly vibe coded to figure out if it is feasible idea)</p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>code</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean.Meta.Tactic.TryThis</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean.Meta.Tactic.TryThis</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MakeHave</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">partial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">leadingIndent</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pos</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String.Pos.Raw</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">go</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String.Pos.Raw</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String.Pos.Raw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i.atEnd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">i</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i.get</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">source</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sc\">' '</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">||</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sc\">'\\t'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">go</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i.next</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">i</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">String.Pos.Raw.extract</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pos</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">go</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pos</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">insertHaveSuggestion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ref</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Syntax</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TacticM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">refRange</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ref.getRange</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instantiateMVars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getMainTarget</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">targetFmt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">withOptions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pp.mvars.set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">withExposedNames</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">PrettyPrinter.ppExpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">target</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">targetText</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">targetFmt.pretty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100000</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fileMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getFileMap</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lineStart</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fileMap.lineStart</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fileMap.toPosition</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">refRange.start</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">line</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">indent</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">leadingIndent</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fileMap.source</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lineStart</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">newText</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"{indent}have : {targetText} := sorry</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">insertionRange</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Syntax.Range</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">lineStart</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lineStart</span><span class=\"o\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">title</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Insert `have` for current goal\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">suggestion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Suggestion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">suggestion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">string</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">newText</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">toCodeActionTitle</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">title</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">addSuggestion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ref</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">suggestion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">origSpan</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Syntax.ofRange</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">insertionRange</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">header</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Code action:\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">Emit a code action inserting `have : &lt;current goal&gt; := sorry` before the current tactic line.</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">This is intended for use as a `simp` discharger, for example:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">`simp (disch:=make_have)`. For `simp` discharger goals, the tactic records the</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">code action and admits the generated side condition so that `simp` can finish.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">The inserted `have` can then discharge later runs via `simp (disch:=assumption)`.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"n\">elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"make_have\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">goal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getMainGoal</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">insertHaveSuggestion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getRef</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">goal.getTag</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`simp.discharger</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">admitGoal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">goal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">synthetic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">disch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">assumption</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">make_have</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MakeHave</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n</div></div>",
        "id": 595417133,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1778889022
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Amazing! Not sure how useful this will be for a bare <code>simp</code> (since it might show <em>many</em> suggestions when not using <code>only</code>), but this will definitely be useful with <code>simp only [curatedSimpSet]</code>, <code>fun_prop</code> or other tactics that allow dischargers.</p>",
        "id": 595441230,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1778902171
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It will always only show one goal, right? The first one it can't discharge?</p>",
        "id": 595441593,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1778902490
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>simp</code> tries to rewrite with many lemmas, and if it fails to apply one lemma (including when it cannot discharge the hypotheses), it just continues with the next lemma (or continues to navigate different sub-expressions). So I suspect the discharger will be called many times and will report all of these (I didn't look at the code, so maybe that is doing something different than I expect?)</p>",
        "id": 595446865,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1778906327
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does it make sense to add <code>field_simp?</code> as notation for </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">field_simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">disch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">default_discharger</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">make_have</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(cc <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"634338\">@Michael Rothgang</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"585783\">@Arend Mellendijk</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"260507\">@Heather Macbeth</span>)</p>",
        "id": 595447171,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1778906616
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"197836\">Jireh Loreaux</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/.60make_have.60.20tacitc/near/595441593\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It will always only show one goal, right? The first one it can't discharge?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>the cool thing is that you can call it recursively and it works perfectly</p>",
        "id": 595451485,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1778910456
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm not sure what this tactic should do if there are bound variables in a side condition that are not in the main local context. Maybe they should be added as an argument to the have?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- This should really be `have (x : Int) : 0 &lt; x`</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">disch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">assumption</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">make_have</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 595489465,
        "sender_full_name": "Arend Mellendijk",
        "timestamp": 1778939602
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also for field_simp specifically the side conditions have a very specific shape, so we could do some processing (and proof caching?) to avoid duplication</p>",
        "id": 595489716,
        "sender_full_name": "Arend Mellendijk",
        "timestamp": 1778939748
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This problem with local variables are not in the original context is a problem I'm thinking about now :) and I agree that all the local variables should be abstracted with forall.</p>\n<p>I see two options:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Make this integral part of simp, fun_prop, ... . then you know the top level context and you can abstract all variables from subgoals not present in the top level context</li>\n<li>Have tactic scope/combinator</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">with_make_have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">dish</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">make_have</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The <code>with_make_have</code> keeps track of the top level scope.</p>\n<p>I'm a bit unsure how to implement this correctly. I would use <code>IO.Ref</code> to communicate between <code>with_make_have</code> and <code>make_have</code> and getting it thread safe will be probably a bit tricky.</p>",
        "id": 595491583,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1778940992
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm writing my own version of <code>apply_rules</code> with bunch of extensions and I'm trying option 1 on it right now. Let's see if it works</p>",
        "id": 595491833,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1778941149
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"585783\">Arend Mellendijk</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/.60make_have.60.20tactic/near/595489716\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Also for field_simp specifically the side conditions have a very specific shape, so we could do some processing (and proof caching?) to avoid duplication</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Not sure what do you mean exactly. If the exact subgoals appears multiple times then it should be suggested only one, right? <code>field_simp</code> will probably want to prove <code>x != 0</code> many, many times and it should show up only once.</p>",
        "id": 595492041,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1778941294
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think you're looking for <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Meta.Simp.Context.lctxInitIndices#doc\">docs#Lean.Meta.Simp.Context.lctxInitIndices</a></p>",
        "id": 595492515,
        "sender_full_name": "Arend Mellendijk",
        "timestamp": 1778941570
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Nice, that is definitely useful information, but a general tactic does not have access to  <code>Simp.Context</code> as it does not live in <code>SimpM</code></p>",
        "id": 595492989,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1778941856
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But yeah if you have <code>lctxInitIndices</code> then I think <code>make_have</code> should just abstract any fvar above that index.</p>",
        "id": 595493348,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1778942051
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, but I see the discharger in <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Meta.Simp.Methods#doc\">docs#Lean.Meta.Simp.Methods</a> lives in SimpM, so this doesn't seem like a fundamental limitation</p>",
        "id": 595493468,
        "sender_full_name": "Arend Mellendijk",
        "timestamp": 1778942126
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes in principle it is possible, it would be great if there was a way to write <code>simp_discharger_decl makeHave : Simp.Discharger := &lt;meta-code&gt;</code> and then be able to write <code>simp [makeHave]</code></p>",
        "id": 595493862,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1778942392
    }
]